1
00:00:00,335 --> 00:00:01,085
At level one,

2
00:00:01,085 --> 00:00:02,935
you trade fifty times a day.

3
00:00:02,935 --> 00:00:03,835
At level ten,

4
00:00:03,835 --> 00:00:05,610
you might trade twice a year.

5
00:00:06,202 --> 00:00:07,877
And the person trading fifty times a

6
00:00:07,877 --> 00:00:08,477
day?

7
00:00:08,452 --> 00:00:10,127
Almost always losing.

8
00:00:10,793 --> 00:00:12,380
This is your life at every level

9
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:13,218
of a trader,

10
00:00:13,218 --> 00:00:14,518
from a thousand dollars,

11
00:00:14,518 --> 00:00:15,693
to a billion.

12
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:21,922
You have a thousand dollars and a

13
00:00:21,922 --> 00:00:23,160
free trading app.

14
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,910
You've watched three videos about candlestick charts

15
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:27,973
You buy at nine thirty.

16
00:00:27,973 --> 00:00:29,110
Sell at nine thirty-four.

17
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:29,985
Buy again.

18
00:00:29,985 --> 00:00:31,885
Your phone buzzes all day.

19
00:00:32,552 --> 00:00:34,039
Some days you're up fifty dollars,

20
00:00:34,039 --> 00:00:35,665
and you feel like a genius.

21
00:00:35,665 --> 00:00:36,327
Most weeks,

22
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:37,252
you're down.

23
00:00:38,027 --> 00:00:39,640
Your biggest risk at this level isn't

24
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:40,240
the market.

25
00:00:40,227 --> 00:00:41,102
It's you.

26
00:00:41,102 --> 00:00:41,889
Boredom.

27
00:00:41,889 --> 00:00:43,789
Revenge trades after a loss.

28
00:00:43,789 --> 00:00:45,802
Trading because the app is open.

29
00:00:46,468 --> 00:00:47,468
The app is free,

30
00:00:47,468 --> 00:00:49,743
so it feels like trading costs nothing

31
00:00:49,843 --> 00:00:51,668
But every time you buy and sell

32
00:00:51,768 --> 00:00:53,318
you pay the gap between the buying

33
00:00:53,318 --> 00:00:55,031
price and the selling price.

34
00:00:55,031 --> 00:00:56,393
Fifty trades a day,

35
00:00:56,393 --> 00:00:57,843
that gap adds up.

36
00:01:00,027 --> 00:01:01,677
You've saved ten thousand.

37
00:01:01,677 --> 00:01:03,252
You want to trade full time.

38
00:01:03,252 --> 00:01:05,289
Then your broker offers you margin.

39
00:01:05,289 --> 00:01:06,077
Borrowed money,

40
00:01:06,077 --> 00:01:07,602
so you can trade bigger.

41
00:01:08,202 --> 00:01:09,502
With two-to-one leverage,

42
00:01:09,502 --> 00:01:11,264
a ten percent drop doesn't cost you

43
00:01:11,264 --> 00:01:12,327
ten percent.

44
00:01:12,327 --> 00:01:13,890
It costs you twenty.

45
00:01:13,890 --> 00:01:15,627
Leverage makes good days better,

46
00:01:15,627 --> 00:01:17,227
and bad days fatal.

47
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:19,298
So you learn the first real rule

48
00:01:19,298 --> 00:01:20,073
of trading.

49
00:01:20,073 --> 00:01:21,035
Survive.

50
00:01:21,827 --> 00:01:23,877
You start writing down every trade,

51
00:01:23,877 --> 00:01:25,139
and why you made it.

52
00:01:25,139 --> 00:01:26,540
Most of your losses come from the

53
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:28,052
same three mistakes.

54
00:01:30,202 --> 00:01:31,477
Twenty-five thousand.

55
00:01:31,477 --> 00:01:32,577
You quit your job.

56
00:01:32,577 --> 00:01:34,677
Your desk now has three monitors.

57
00:01:35,268 --> 00:01:36,868
Here's what the data says about this

58
00:01:36,868 --> 00:01:37,605
level.

59
00:01:37,605 --> 00:01:40,343
Researchers followed everyone who started day trading

60
00:01:40,343 --> 00:01:43,493
Brazil's stock futures market between twenty thirteen

61
00:01:43,493 --> 00:01:44,893
and twenty fifteen.

62
00:01:45,527 --> 00:01:46,752
Of those who kept at it for

63
00:01:46,752 --> 00:01:48,564
more than three hundred days,

64
00:01:48,564 --> 00:01:50,865
ninety-seven percent lost money.

65
00:01:50,865 --> 00:01:52,714
Only about one in a hundred earned

66
00:01:52,714 --> 00:01:54,402
more than the minimum wage.

67
00:01:55,227 --> 00:01:55,827
Your day:

68
00:01:55,702 --> 00:01:56,602
wake at six,

69
00:01:56,602 --> 00:01:57,427
read the news,

70
00:01:57,427 --> 00:01:58,302
wait for the open,

71
00:01:58,302 --> 00:01:59,365
trade the first hour,

72
00:01:59,365 --> 00:02:00,427
then try not to give it all

73
00:02:00,427 --> 00:02:01,714
back by lunch.

74
00:02:01,714 --> 00:02:02,739
No salary.

75
00:02:02,739 --> 00:02:03,827
No sick pay.

76
00:02:03,827 --> 00:02:05,702
Your income is whatever the market lets

77
00:02:05,702 --> 00:02:06,552
you keep.

78
00:02:08,727 --> 00:02:09,852
A hundred thousand.

79
00:02:09,852 --> 00:02:11,177
But it isn't yours.

80
00:02:11,793 --> 00:02:12,793
You paid a fee to take a

81
00:02:12,793 --> 00:02:14,693
trading test at a prop firm.

82
00:02:14,693 --> 00:02:15,681
You passed.

83
00:02:15,681 --> 00:02:17,081
Now you trade the firm's money,

84
00:02:17,081 --> 00:02:18,743
and keep a share of the profits

85
00:02:19,527 --> 00:02:20,677
Break their rules,

86
00:02:20,677 --> 00:02:22,277
like losing too much in one day

87
00:02:22,352 --> 00:02:23,852
and the account is gone.

88
00:02:24,627 --> 00:02:25,927
The firm doesn't need you to be

89
00:02:25,927 --> 00:02:26,877
a genius.

90
00:02:26,877 --> 00:02:28,602
It needs you to not blow up

91
00:02:28,715 --> 00:02:30,202
Most of the job is the boring

92
00:02:30,202 --> 00:02:30,802
part:

93
00:02:30,790 --> 00:02:31,727
small bets,

94
00:02:31,727 --> 00:02:32,464
tight stops,

95
00:02:32,464 --> 00:02:34,602
and walking away after a bad morning

96
00:02:36,893 --> 00:02:37,493
A million.

97
00:02:37,418 --> 00:02:39,043
You're on a bank's trading desk now

98
00:02:39,143 --> 00:02:39,743
A suit.

99
00:02:39,618 --> 00:02:40,293
A badge.

100
00:02:40,293 --> 00:02:41,768
A daily loss limit.

101
00:02:42,393 --> 00:02:43,868
Your salary is good.

102
00:02:43,868 --> 00:02:45,843
Your bonus depends on your profits.

103
00:02:45,843 --> 00:02:47,755
And everything you do is recorded and

104
00:02:47,755 --> 00:02:48,518
checked.

105
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,310
Risk managers watch your positions.

106
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:53,210
Compliance reads your messages.

107
00:02:53,210 --> 00:02:54,498
If you hit your loss limit,

108
00:02:54,498 --> 00:02:55,798
you stop for the day.

109
00:02:55,798 --> 00:02:57,060
No arguments.

110
00:02:57,727 --> 00:02:59,502
This is the level where rogue traders

111
00:02:59,502 --> 00:03:00,252
appear.

112
00:03:00,252 --> 00:03:01,677
People who hide a loss,

113
00:03:01,677 --> 00:03:03,477
then bet bigger to win it back

114
00:03:03,615 --> 00:03:04,927
In nineteen ninety-five,

115
00:03:04,927 --> 00:03:05,527
one of them,

116
00:03:05,427 --> 00:03:06,290
Nick Leeson,

117
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:07,302
sank Barings,

118
00:03:07,302 --> 00:03:09,277
Britain's oldest merchant bank.

119
00:03:11,468 --> 00:03:12,218
Ten million.

120
00:03:12,218 --> 00:03:13,581
You're a portfolio manager.

121
00:03:13,581 --> 00:03:14,843
It's other people's money.

122
00:03:14,843 --> 00:03:15,443
Pensions.

123
00:03:15,430 --> 00:03:16,443
Families.

124
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:19,235
You stop staring at one-minute charts.

125
00:03:19,235 --> 00:03:20,960
You think in weeks and months.

126
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:22,410
You trade a few times a week

127
00:03:22,460 --> 00:03:24,135
not a few times an hour.

128
00:03:24,927 --> 00:03:26,502
Your job isn't to be right every

129
00:03:26,502 --> 00:03:27,152
day.

130
00:03:27,152 --> 00:03:28,452
It's to be right more often than

131
00:03:28,452 --> 00:03:29,052
you're wrong,

132
00:03:29,027 --> 00:03:30,877
and to lose small when you're wrong

133
00:03:31,015 --> 00:03:32,902
A good year might be ten percent

134
00:03:33,002 --> 00:03:33,952
On ten million,

135
00:03:33,952 --> 00:03:35,677
that's a million dollars.

136
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:39,035
A hundred million.

137
00:03:39,035 --> 00:03:41,035
You've started your own hedge fund.

138
00:03:41,635 --> 00:03:43,860
The classic deal is two and twenty

139
00:03:44,023 --> 00:03:45,885
Two percent of the money every year

140
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,810
and twenty percent of the profits.

141
00:03:48,427 --> 00:03:49,702
On a hundred million,

142
00:03:49,702 --> 00:03:51,627
that two percent is two million dollars

143
00:03:51,627 --> 00:03:52,352
a year,

144
00:03:52,352 --> 00:03:54,427
before you've made a single trade.

145
00:03:55,218 --> 00:03:56,643
You hire analysts.

146
00:03:56,643 --> 00:03:58,268
You spend half your time talking to

147
00:03:58,268 --> 00:03:59,231
investors.

148
00:03:59,231 --> 00:04:01,293
A bad year doesn't just cost money

149
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:03,006
Clients can pull their money out,

150
00:04:03,006 --> 00:04:04,993
and the fund can shrink overnight.

151
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:07,885
A billion.

152
00:04:07,885 --> 00:04:08,485
Now,

153
00:04:08,185 --> 00:04:09,885
your trades move the market.

154
00:04:10,502 --> 00:04:12,102
If you try to buy too fast

155
00:04:12,202 --> 00:04:14,252
you push the price up against yourself

156
00:04:14,365 --> 00:04:15,977
A big position can take weeks to

157
00:04:15,977 --> 00:04:16,602
build,

158
00:04:16,602 --> 00:04:17,927
a little at a time.

159
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,460
So you need fewer,

160
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:20,060
bigger,

161
00:04:19,885 --> 00:04:21,160
better ideas.

162
00:04:21,927 --> 00:04:22,677
At this size,

163
00:04:22,677 --> 00:04:23,702
you have a team,

164
00:04:23,702 --> 00:04:24,815
a risk committee,

165
00:04:24,815 --> 00:04:25,415
lawyers,

166
00:04:25,315 --> 00:04:27,489
and brokers competing for your business.

167
00:04:27,489 --> 00:04:29,477
Your edge is no longer speed.

168
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:31,952
It's thinking further ahead than everybody else

169
00:04:34,318 --> 00:04:35,906
Level nine is the legend.

170
00:04:35,906 --> 00:04:36,643
One idea,

171
00:04:36,643 --> 00:04:37,768
sized to win.

172
00:04:38,418 --> 00:04:40,281
In September nineteen ninety-two,

173
00:04:40,281 --> 00:04:42,368
George Soros's fund bet that the British

174
00:04:42,368 --> 00:04:43,668
pound would crash.

175
00:04:43,668 --> 00:04:44,568
It did.

176
00:04:44,568 --> 00:04:46,568
The bet reportedly made about a billion

177
00:04:46,568 --> 00:04:47,543
dollars.

178
00:04:48,335 --> 00:04:50,235
But for every famous winning bet,

179
00:04:50,235 --> 00:04:51,735
there are funds that bet big,

180
00:04:51,735 --> 00:04:52,335
were wrong,

181
00:04:52,297 --> 00:04:53,485
and disappeared.

182
00:04:55,635 --> 00:04:57,760
And level ten barely trades at all

183
00:04:58,552 --> 00:05:00,727
Warren Buffett once wrote that his favourite

184
00:05:00,727 --> 00:05:02,527
holding period is forever.

185
00:05:03,268 --> 00:05:04,618
He buys a company and holds it

186
00:05:04,618 --> 00:05:05,243
for years,

187
00:05:05,243 --> 00:05:06,656
sometimes decades.

188
00:05:06,656 --> 00:05:08,631
No screens flashing all day.

189
00:05:08,631 --> 00:05:09,231
Mostly,

190
00:05:09,068 --> 00:05:09,818
reading.

191
00:05:10,593 --> 00:05:12,243
So look at the ladder again.

192
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:13,472
At the bottom,

193
00:05:13,472 --> 00:05:14,348
the most trades,

194
00:05:14,348 --> 00:05:15,098
the least money,

195
00:05:15,098 --> 00:05:16,560
and the worst results.

196
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:17,435
At the top,

197
00:05:17,435 --> 00:05:18,372
the fewest trades,

198
00:05:18,372 --> 00:05:19,685
and the biggest money.

199
00:05:20,327 --> 00:05:22,027
Every trade costs something.

200
00:05:22,027 --> 00:05:22,627
Fees,

201
00:05:22,477 --> 00:05:23,077
spreads,

202
00:05:22,915 --> 00:05:23,702
mistakes.

203
00:05:23,702 --> 00:05:25,227
The traders who last learn to do

204
00:05:25,227 --> 00:05:26,027
less.

205
00:05:26,718 --> 00:05:28,593
Most people start at level one and

206
00:05:28,593 --> 00:05:30,193
try to trade their way up.

207
00:05:30,193 --> 00:05:31,418
The ones at the top got there

208
00:05:31,418 --> 00:05:32,768
by trading less.

